      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This “Armistice Day Prayer” was composed in 1923 by the Office of the Chief Rabbi on the Anniversary of the cessation of conflict on November 11th marking the end of the Great War (later known as World War I). The prayer was likely written by Rabbi Joseph Herman Hertz who had been elected Chief Rabbi in 1913.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>We are grateful to Jeffrey Maynard and his blog, Jewish Miscellanies, for sharing page images of this prayer.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
